  "statuteText": "659:29 Special Provisions for State and Presidential Primary Elections. –\n\nAny voter at any state or presidential primary election may challenge any other voter offering to declare himself as a member of a party or to vote the ballot of a party. Such challenged voter shall not be allowed to so declare or so vote until he makes an oath or affirmation that he affiliates with and generally supports the candidates of the party."
